# Public HTTPS URL of a Midnight proof server.
#
# A FALLBACK, not an override. In live mode (#/live) the proof server URL comes
# from Lace's own getConfiguration(), because Lace is the process that has to
# reach it. This is used only when the connected wallet reports none -- e.g. a
# build that ships its own tunnelled proof server.
#
# It has no effect on the #/app simulation, which runs circuits unproven in
# memory and needs no prover at all.
#
# In the devcontainer, start the proof server and expose it:
#   docker compose -f proof-server/docker-compose.yml up -d
#   .devcontainer/tunnel.sh
# then copy the printed URL here (as ui/.env.local, which is gitignored).
#
# Must be https:// if the page itself is served over https, or the browser
# blocks it as mixed content.
# VITE_PROOF_SERVER_URL=https://example.trycloudflare.com

# ── Live on-chain mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The address printed by `cli/npm run deploy`, also written to
# cli/.deployments/<network>.json. Without it #/live can only deploy a new
# market, the landing page shows no on-chain figures, and the market grid falls
# back to its illustrative copy.
# VITE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# Must match BOTH the network Lace is set to and the network the contract above
# was deployed on. preview and preprod are separate chains: an address deployed
# on one does not exist on the other, and the indexer will simply report no such
# contract.
# VITE_NETWORK_ID=preview
#
# The indexer URL is derived from this (src/lib/network.ts) and is queried
# without a wallet, which is how the landing page shows real on-chain counts to
# a visitor who has installed nothing.
